This standard provides guidelines to make dispersions from powder/liquid combinations. It provides procedures for:
a) Wetting a powder into a liquid;
b) Deagglomerating the wetted clumps;
c) Determining if solution composition can be adjusted to prevent reagglomeration;
d) Selecting dispersing agents to prevent reagglomeration; and
e) Evaluating the stability of the dispersion against reagglomeration.
This standard is applicable to particles ranging in size from approximately 0.05 µm to 100 µm. It provides a series of questions on the nature of the powder and liquid involved. The answers are used with charts that guide the user to generic dispersing agents that are likely to be suitable for dispersing the powder in the liquid. This standard applies only to the preparation of simple, dilute dispersions (less than 1 percent by volume of solids) for particle size analysis.

